# libreadline

`libreadline` is the r10 owner of `libreadline.so.8`. It depends exactly on
the wide-character ncurses provider required by the reviewed Buildroot recipe.
The feed intentionally does not silently package the separate history library:
it is not needed by the initial `gawk` target and must receive its own owner if
a later candidate needs it.

The source lock includes both GNU Readline and the ncurses archive because
Buildroot's readline path can prepare ncurses/host-ncurses as part of a clean,
offline library build.
